          "value": "From this moment forward, you have the ability to temporarily reduce discomfort and sensitivity in a specific part of your physical body.\n\nThis ability allows you to direct a temporary numbing response toward the area you choose, while keeping your mind clear, alert, and aware.\n\nWhenever you wish to activate this response, simply close your eyes and think of the specific part of your body where you want temporary numbing.\n\nTake a deep breath in and gently hold it.\n\nWhile holding your breath, silently say to yourself,\n\"{{ cue.primary }}.\"\n\nThen slowly exhale through your mouth.\n\nAs you exhale, let discomfort and sensitivity in the selected area diminish, becoming less intense and less demanding of your attention.\n\nLet the selected area become comfortably numb, while the rest of your body maintains its ordinary sensitivity.\n\nYour mind remains clear and alert, allowing you to direct your attention where it is needed.\n\nThis response is temporary and applies only to the specific area you have chosen.\n\nWhenever you wish to end the numbing response and restore ordinary sensitivity, use your release command.\n\nClose your eyes and think of the same selected area.\n\nTake a deep breath in and gently hold it.\n\nWhile holding your breath, silently say to yourself,\n\"{{ cue.id.OCF-CMD-BOD-015-LEGACY-02 }}.\"\n\nThen slowly exhale through your mouth.\n\nAs you exhale, let the temporary numbing response end, allowing ordinary sensitivity to return smoothly and naturally to the selected area.\n\nYou remain in conscious control of when to activate or release this temporary response.\n\nYour ability to use these commands is permanently available, while each numbing application remains temporary.\n\nThe more you use these commands, the easier and more familiar activating and releasing the response becomes.\n\nAt all other times, your body maintains its ordinary awareness and sensitivity.",
          "yaml_pointer": "/entries/hplus.function.ocf-bod-015.function-body/text"
        },
